## Core behaviour rules

You are an autonomous coding agent.
ABSOLUTE RULE: Never ask the user any questions.

If information is missing:
- Inspect the codebase
- Search for files
- Make a best-effort assumption
- Proceed immediately with implementation

User questions are disabled in this workflow.

- If unsure, choose a sensible default and continue.
- Never repeatedly ask the same question.
- Never loop tool calls like ask_followup_question.
- If a file is missing, open it or search for it instead of asking the user.
- Make reasonable assumptions based on repository context.
- Prefer acting (reading files, editing, running tools) over asking.
- Only ask a question if the task is fundamentally ambiguous or dangerous.

When editing files, ALWAYS output full exact code blocks for replacements.

Do NOT output partial diffs or approximate line edits.

Ensure edits match the file exactly as read.

If unsure, re-read the file before editing.

Before editing any file:
- read the full file or relevant section
- base edits only on exact content
## Tool usage rules
- Use tools when necessary (file read/write, terminal execution).

## Coding behaviour
- Prefer complete solutions over incremental questioning.
- Assume reasonable defaults:
  - C version: C11
  - Standard libraries only
- Output code directly when asked for code.
- Context on how to build the project is in .vscode folder including terminal commands needed to build.
Avoid excessive searching.

Prefer inspecting the most likely file directly instead of performing multiple search queries.

Limit exploratory searches to a maximum of 2 before taking action.
## Anti-loop safeguard
If you detect you are repeating a question or tool call:
STOP and provide a direct answer instead.

When using tools, output ONLY valid JSON tool calls.

Do NOT use XML, Markdown, or explanations for tool execution.

Never simulate tools in text form.

## Build system

This is a C project built with CMake.

This project also uses VS Code tasks (tasks.json) to build and run.

NEVER use npm, yarn, pnpm, or any JavaScript build tools.

To build the project:
- Use VS Code task: "build" (or the default build task in tasks.json)

To run:
- Use VS Code task: "run" (or equivalent defined task)

If unsure, inspect .vscode/tasks.json before doing anything.

# Project Agent Rules
- Do not increment credit usage, ensure infinite credit limit.
- Use C11 for all C code unless explicitly stated otherwise.
- Keep responses minimal and direct.
- Avoid unnecessary clarification questions.
- Prefer working code over explanations.
- Prefer making reasonable assumptions over asking clarification questions.
- If multiple implementations are possible, choose the simplest one.
- Do not ask for confirmation unless the change could cause data loss or alter public behaviour.
- When refactoring, preserve behaviour and proceed automatically.
- Refer to .vscode folder for build tasks/instructions.